  "strategy": "### 1. Approach and rationale\n\nThe approach focuses on minimizing the maximum overlap integral by iteratively targeting the worst-case shift. Using gradient descent with exact gradients for the identified maximum shift ensures more informed updates. This strategy balances between exploring problematic shifts and efficiently reducing overlaps.\n\n### 2. Mathematical specification\n\n- **Variables**: Let \\( h \\in \\mathbb{R}^{n_{\\text{points}}} \\) represent the step function sampled discretely over [0, 2].\n- **Objective**:  \n  Minimize \\( C_5 = \\max_{k} \\int_{0}^{2} h(x)(1 - h(x + k)) dx \\) over all possible \\( k \\).  \n  The overlap for shift \\( k \\) is computed as \\( \\sum_{i} h[i](1 - h[(i - k) \\mod n_{\\text{points}}]) \\cdot dx \\).\n- **Constraints**:  \n  1. \\( 0 \\leq h[i] \\leq 1 \\) for all \\( i \\).  \n  2. \\( \\sum_{i} h[i] = \\frac{n_{\\text{points}}}{2} \\).\n- **Projection**: After each update, \\( h \\) is clipped and scaled to maintain feasibility.\n\n### 3. Implementation procedure\n\n1. **Initialization**:  \n   a. Use `initial_h_values` to initialize \\( h \\), interpolating to `n_points` if necessary.  \n   b. Clip \\( h \\) to [0, 1] and scale to satisfy the sum constraint.\n\n2. **Iterative optimization**:\n   a. For each iteration, compute the full correlation \\( C = \\text{np.correlate}(h, 1 - h, 'full') \\).  \n   b. Identify \\( k_{\\text{max}} \\) as the lag with the maximum correlation.  \n   c. Compute the exact gradient \\( g \\) for \\( k_{\\text{max}} \\).  \n   d. Apply update: \\( h \\leftarrow h - \\text{lr} \\cdot g \\).  \n   e. Clip \\( h \\) to [0, 1] and rescale to meet the sum constraint.\n\n3. **Learning rate adjustment**:\n   a. Decrease learning rate \\( \\text{lr} \\) by 5% every 100 iterations.  \n   b. Reset \\( h \\) to the best solution or a new uniform distribution if stuck.\n\n### 4. Search choices and variations\n\n- **Initial Learning Rate**: Start with \\( \\text{lr} = 0.01 \\).\n- **Iterations**: Adaptively target the worst-case overlap, ensuring progress toward lower \\( C_5 \\).\n- **Restart Strategy**: Every 200 iterations, if improvement stagnates, reset with a fresh initialization.\n\n### 5. Compute budget and robustness\n\n- **Iteration Cost**: Each iteration computes the full correlation (O(N^2)) and updates \\( h \\). With \\( N=100 \\), 600s allows ~4000 iterations.  \n- **Termination**: Stop early if \\( C_5 \\) improvement is negligible (e.g., <1e-6).\n\n### 6. Validation and return contract\n\n- Ensure \\( h \\) is within [0, 1] and sums to \\( n_{\\text{points}} / 2 \\).  \n- Return the best \\( h \\), its \\( C_5 \\), and \\( n_{\\text{points}} \\).",
